{
  "about": [
    "The Plan View's rules, written as data: the three heaps a planning pass splits the Tasks into,",
    "which bound a move would break, the scope one rung up, and where work taken out lands.",
    "",
    "Both evaluators replay it. `src-tauri/tests/operations/plan_triage_conformance.rs` runs every case",
    "through `tasks::rules::plan` — whose bounds are the writer's own containment check; and",
    "`src/utils/plan-triage-conformance.test.ts` runs them through `plan-triage.ts`,",
    "`plan-take-out.ts` and `parentRefs`. Neither side generates this file.",
    "",
    "A row names its own `timeScope` and `plan` (scope keys, as `scope-keys.json` spells them), the",
    "`inheritedPlan` the board serves it (its parent's effective Plan clipped to its window, see",
    "`docs/spec/time-scopes.md`, *Plan inheritance*), whether that came to nothing (`emptyPlan`),",
    "whether it is `overdue`, whether it is a drawing with no row (`virtual`), and its `ancestors`,",
    "outermost first, each with its kind and own Time Scope. `triage` lists each heap's rows",
    "in row order for a `target` scope whose `parent` is given (null for a Season); a row in none of",
    "them is planned elsewhere, irrelevant, or a drawing. `refusals` names the bound a move into",
    "`target` breaks, or null. `parents` gives the scope one rung up; `takeOut` says where work taken",
    "out of a scope lands — the scope `filled`, its `parent`, or `clear`.",
    "",
    "`sections` splits the rows planned into `target` into one bucket per part one rung down, each",
    "with whether it reaches outside the scope (`partial`) and its rows, plus the rows no bucket holds;",
    "an empty Premorning is left out unless `includePremorning`. `scopes` gives the first and last day",
    "of every scope those cases name, as `ScopeKey::scope` derives them."
  ],
